          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Nisnevich topology
            is a certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+topology"} Zariski topology
            but coarser than the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+topology"} étale topology
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The Nisnevich
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomological+dimension"} cohomological dimension
                (and even the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+dimension"} homotopy dimension
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krull+dimension"} Krull dimension
                (like Zariski)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} Fields
                have
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} trivial shape
                for the Nisnevich topology (like Zariski)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} Algebraic K-theory
                satisfies
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
                over the Nisnevich site – as is true for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+site"} Zariski site
                but not in full generality for the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+site"} etale site
                %em
                  %a{:href => "algebraic%20K-theory#Descent"} algebraic K-theory – Descent
                for more;
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z\subset X
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subscheme"} closed immersion
                between affine schemes that are smooth over a base
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo −
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/(X-Z)
                is isomorphic to
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mrow
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mrow
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Z
                        %mo −
                        %mi Z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_{X,Z}/(N_{X,Z}-Z)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_{X,Z}
                is the normal bundle of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                (like étale)
            %li
              %p
                Pushforward along a
                %span.newWikiWord
                  finite morphism
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/finite+morphism"} ?
                is an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} exact functor
                on Nisnevich sheaves of abelian groups (like étale)
            %li
              %p
                Nisnevich cohomology can be computed using
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+cohomology"} Čech cohomology
                (like étale)
          %p
            The Nisnevich topology plays a central role in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+homotopy+theory"} motivic homotopy theory
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            An family of morphisms of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noetherian+scheme"} Noetherian scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{p_i:V_i\to U\}
            is a
            %strong Nisnevich cover
            if each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_i
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+map"} étale map
            and if every field-valued point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec k\to U
            lifts to one of the
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_i
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopology"} pretopology
            on the category of Noetherian schemes, and the associated topology is the
            = succeed "." do
              %strong Nisnevich topology
          %p
            The
            %strong Nisnevich site
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noetherian+scheme"} Noetherian scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            usually refers to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+scheme"} smooth scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            equipped with the Nisnevich topology. The
            %strong small Nisnevich site
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is the subsite consisting of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+map"} étale
            = succeed "-schemes." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %h3#for_nonnoetherian_schemes For non-Noetherian schemes
          %p
            For a general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+scheme"} affine scheme
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to be a covering sieve for the Nisnevich topology if there exist a Noetherian affine scheme
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: X\to Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast(T)\subset S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a Nisnevich covering sieve if there exists an open cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i\to X\}
            by affine schemes such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{/U_i}
            is a Nisnevich covering sieve on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
          %h3#as_an_excision_property As an excision property
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Et
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Et/S
            be the category of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+scheme"} étale scheme
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism+of+finite+presentation"} finite presentation
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-compact+morphism"} quasi-compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-separated+morphism"} quasi-separated
            scheme
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaf"} (∞,1)-presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Et
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Et/S
            is said to satisfy
            %em Nisnevich excision
            if the following conditions hold:
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(\emptyset)
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible"} contractible
            %li
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
              is a closed subscheme of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Et
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in Et/S
              and if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X'\to X
              is a morphism in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Et
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Et/S
              which is an isomorphism over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo −
                          %mi Z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ′
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi Z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  F(X) &amp;\to&amp; F(X-Z)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  F(X') &amp;\to&amp; F(X'-Z)
                  }
          %p
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
            square. Intuitively, this says that the space of sections of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with support in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            (i.e., the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
            of
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo −
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(X) \to F(X-Z)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#DAGXI"} DAG XI
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaf"} (∞,1)-presheaf
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Et
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Et/S
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf"} (∞,1)-sheaf
              for the Nisnevich topology if and only if it satisifes Nisnevich excision.
          %p
            This is
            %a{:href => "#MV99"} Morel-Voevosky, Prop. 1.16
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#DAGXI"} DAG XI, Thm. 2.9
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#homotopy_dimension Homotopy dimension
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noetherian+scheme"} Noetherian scheme
              of finite
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krull+dimension"} Krull dimension
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-sheaves
              on the small Nisnevich site of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              has
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+dimension"} homotopy dimension
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi dim
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq\dim(S)
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#DAGXI"} DAG XI, Theorem 2.24
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Postnikov+tower"} Postnikov tower
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-sheaves
            on the Nisnevich site over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercomplete"} hypercomplete
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              More generally, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is a pro-algebraic space limit of a cofiltered diagram of qcqs algebraic spaces of Krull dimension
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq d
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-sheaves
              on the small Nisnevich site of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              has
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+dimension"} homotopy dimension
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq d
          %p This is Clausen and A. Mathew, Hyperdescent and etale K-theory, 2019, arXiv:1905.06611, Cor.3.11, Thm.3.12, and Thm.3.17.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fpqc-site"} fpqc-site
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fppf-site"} fppf-site
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntomic+site"} syntomic site
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+site"} étale site
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
                %strong Nisnevich site
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+site"} Zariski site
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cd-structure"} cd-structure
          %h2#references References
          %p A quick overview is at the beginning of the talk slides
          %ul
            %li
              Jardine,
              %em Motivic spaces and the motivic stable category
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.aimath.org/WWN/motivesdessins/motivic.pdf"}> pdf
              ) .
          %p
            A detailed discussion is in
            %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0305/nowmovo.pdf#page=61"} section 3.1.1
            of
          %ul#MV99
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fabien+Morel"}> Fabien Morel
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Voevodsky"} Vladimir Voevodsky
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔸
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}^1
                \-homotopy theory of schemes
              , K-theory, 0305 (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0305/"} web
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0305/nowmovo.pdf"} pdf
          %p or in the lecture notes
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Friedlander"}> Eric Friedlander
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.northwestern.edu/~eric/lectures/"} Algebraic Cycles and algebraic K-theory, II
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.northwestern.edu/~eric/lectures/ihp/ihplec6.pdf"}> lecture 6 (pdf)
              )
          %p
            A self-contained account of the Nisnevich
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %ul#DAGXI
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em Derived Algebraic Geometry XI: Descent Theorems
